[ Desmond Morris ](/wiki/Desmond_Morris "Desmond Morris") in [ The Naked Ape
](/wiki/The_Naked_Ape "The Naked Ape") and [ The Human Zoo
](/wiki/The_Human_Zoo_\(book\) "The Human Zoo \(book\)") , [ Robert Ardrey
](/wiki/Robert_Ardrey "Robert Ardrey") in [ African Genesis
](/wiki/African_Genesis "African Genesis") and [ Konrad Lorenz
](/wiki/Konrad_Lorenz "Konrad Lorenz") in [ On Aggression
](/wiki/On_Aggression "On Aggression") all wrote from a [ sociobiological
](/wiki/Sociobiological "Sociobiological") perspective. They viewed the human
species as an animal, subject to the evolutionary law of [ Survival of the
fittest ](/wiki/Survival_of_the_fittest "Survival of the fittest") through
adaptation to the [ biophysical environment ](/wiki/Biophysical_environment
"Biophysical environment") .  [6]

