RCTs are considered to be the most reliable form of [ scientific evidence
](/wiki/Scientific_method "Scientific method") in the [ hierarchy of evidence
](/wiki/Hierarchy_of_evidence "Hierarchy of evidence") that influences
healthcare policy and practice because RCTs reduce spurious causality and
bias. Results of RCTs may be combined in [ systematic reviews
](/wiki/Systematic_review "Systematic review") which are increasingly being
used in the conduct of [ evidence-based practice ](/wiki/Evidence-
based_practice "Evidence-based practice") . Some examples of scientific
